---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import LegalPage from '../components/LegalPage.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = '1 November 2026';
const toc = [
  { id: 'what-are-cookies', label: 'What cookies are' },
  { id: 'our-position', label: 'Our position' },
  { id: 'cookies-we-use', label: 'Cookies that may be set' },
  { id: 'what-we-do-not-use', label: 'What we do not use' },
  { id: 'browser-storage', label: 'Browser storage' },
  { id: 'third-party', label: 'Third-party destinations' },
  { id: 'managing', label: 'Managing cookies' },
  { id: 'consent', label: 'Consent position' },
  { id: 'changes', label: 'Changes' },
  { id: 'contact', label: 'Contact' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy"
  description="Which cookies China Filter Hub does and does not use: no advertising or analytics tracking, only the security cookies our content delivery network may set."
  breadcrumbs={[{ label: 'Cookie Policy', href: '/cookies/' }]}
  updated="2026-11-01"
>
  <LegalPage
    title="Cookie Policy"
    updated={updated}
    toc={toc}
    intro="This page lists the cookies and similar technologies that may be used when you visit chinafilterhub.com, what each one does, and how you can control them. It should be read together with our Privacy Policy."
  >
    <h2 id="what-are-cookies">1. What cookies are</h2>
    <p>
      A cookie is a small text file that a website asks your browser to store. It is sent back to
      the same site on later requests, which lets the site remember something between page views —
      for example, that a security challenge has already been passed. Cookies can be
      <em>first-party</em> (set by the site you are visiting) or <em>third-party</em> (set by
      another domain whose resource is loaded by the page).
    </p>
    <p>
      Related technologies include local storage, session storage and pixels. They work in
      comparable ways and are treated the same way in this policy.
    </p>

    <h2 id="our-position">2. Our position</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a business-to-business information resource. It does not carry advertising, does
      not run audience analytics, and does not embed social plugins or tracking pixels. There is
      therefore no cookie banner on the site, because there is no non-essential cookie to ask you
      about.
    </p>
    <p>
      The only cookies that may be present are set by our content delivery network for security and
      abuse prevention. They do not identify you to us, are not used to build a profile, and are not
      shared for advertising.
    </p>

    <h2 id="cookies-we-use">3. Cookies that may be set</h2>
    <p>
      The site is delivered through Cloudflare. Depending on traffic conditions and whether a
      security check is triggered, Cloudflare may set one or more of the following:
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table class="data">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th scope="col">Cookie</th>
            <th scope="col">Set by</th>
            <th scope="col">Purpose</th>
            <th scope="col">Typical lifetime</th>
            <th scope="col">Category</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td><code>__cf_bm</code></td>
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Distinguishes human visitors from automated traffic, so that bots cannot degrade the site or abuse forms.</td>
            <td>About 30 minutes</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary — security</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>cf_clearance</code></td>
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Records that a visitor has passed a security challenge, so the challenge is not repeated on every request.</td>
            <td>For the duration of the clearance period</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary — security</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>_cfuvid</code></td>
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Supports rate limiting and bot detection at the edge.</td>
            <td>Session</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary — security</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td><code>cf_chl_*</code></td>
            <td>Cloudflare</td>
            <td>Short-lived values used while a security challenge is being completed.</td>
            <td>Minutes</td>
            <td>Strictly necessary — security</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="muted small">
      Whether a particular cookie appears depends on your request and on the security settings
      applied to the site at that moment. You can inspect the cookies actually set in your browser
      using its developer tools.
    </p>

    <h2 id="what-we-do-not-use">4. What we do not use</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>No analytics cookies</strong> — the site does not load Google Analytics, Plausible, Umami, Matomo or any comparable product.</li>
      <li><strong>No advertising or retargeting cookies</strong> — no advertising pixels, no conversion tracking, no remarketing audiences.</li>
      <li><strong>No social media plugins</strong> — no embedded like buttons, feeds or share widgets that would contact a third party before you click.</li>
      <li><strong>No session or login cookies</strong> — there are no accounts, no shopping cart and no checkout on this site.</li>
      <li><strong>No cross-site tracking</strong> — we do not attempt to recognise you across other websites.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="browser-storage">5. Browser storage</h2>
    <p>
      The site does not write to local storage or session storage, and does not read or set
      first-party cookies through script. The quotation form is composed entirely in your browser
      and opens a message in your own email client; nothing is saved locally by the site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="third-party">6. Third-party destinations</h2>
    <p>
      Some pages contain ordinary links to external services — for example a WhatsApp click-to-chat
      link, or a citation to Baidu Baike. Following a link takes you to that service, which may then
      set its own cookies under its own policy. Because those are links rather than embedded
      widgets, no third-party cookie is set while you are simply reading this site.
    </p>

    <h2 id="managing">7. Managing cookies</h2>
    <p>
      You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Because the cookies described
      above are used for security, blocking them may cause a security check to reappear more often,
      or may prevent access to the site entirely if you block all first-party cookies.
    </p>
    <p>
      Most browsers also offer a private or incognito mode, which discards cookies when the window
      closes. Browser help pages describe the exact menu path for each product.
    </p>

    <h2 id="consent">8. Consent position</h2>
    <p>
      Under the ePrivacy Directive and the UK Privacy and Electronic Communications Regulations,
      consent is required for non-essential cookies. This site sets no non-essential cookies, so no
      consent request is shown. If we introduce analytics or advertising in future, we will update
      this page and add a consent mechanism before those cookies are set.
    </p>
    <p>
      Because we do not track or sell personal information, Do Not Track and Global Privacy Control
      signals do not change the site&rsquo;s behaviour: the site already does not do what those
      signals are intended to prevent.
    </p>

    <h2 id="changes">9. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We review this page whenever the site&rsquo;s technology changes. The date at the top shows
      the current version. Any future addition of analytics or advertising would be reflected here
      before it went live.
    </p>

    <h2 id="contact">10. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${site.entity.email}`}>{site.entity.email}</a> ·{' '}
      <a href={`mailto:${site.entity.emailAlt}`}>{site.entity.emailAlt}</a> · {site.entity.phone}
    </p>
    <p class="muted small">
      See also: <a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a> · <a href="/terms/">Terms of Service</a> ·{' '}
      <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a> · <a href="/company/">Company details</a>
    </p>
  </LegalPage>
</BaseLayout>
